  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Court On Its Own Motion vs The State Government Through The Chief ... on 11 September, 2024 Author: Sujit Narayan Prasad Bench: Sujit Narayan Prasad In The High Court Of Jharkhand At Ranchi W.P.(Pil) No.171 of 2012 ----- Court on its own motion ... ... ... Petitioner Versus 1. The State Government through the Chief Secretary, Government of Jharkhand. 2. Principal Secretary, Animal Husbandry Department, Government of Jharkhand. 3. Principal Home Secretary, Government of Jharkhand. ... ... ... Respondents ------- Coram:Hon'Blethe Acting Chief Justice Hon'Blemr. Justice Arun Kumar Rai ------- Amicus Curiae :Mr. Piyush Poddar, Adv. For the Resp-State : Mr. Manish Kumar, Sr. SC-II : Ms. Sunita Kumar, AC to Sr. SC-II For the Resp. J.P.S.C. & J.S.S.C. :Mr. Sanjoy Piprawall, Advocate : Mr. Rakesh Ranjan, Advocate : Mr. Prince Kumar, Advocate : Mr. Jay Prakash, Advocate ------",
    "facts": "It is a case where the recruitment process of the Food Safety Officer had begun in the year 2023 and thewritten examination has also been conducted, but the result has not yet been published.",
    "arguments": "2. It has been contended by learned Amicus that for one reason or the other, it is the J.P.S.C. who is not publishing the result on the ground of some clarification which the J.P.S.C. is seeking from the State. 5. This Court is of the view that once the requisition has been made on the basis of Rule in vogue based upon that Advertisement has been notified reflecting the total number of vacancies, there is no reason for the JPSC not to come out with the result based upon the performance of one or the other candidates who participated in the process of selection. 8. Learned counsel appearing for the State has submitted that the requisition has already been made to the Staff Selection Commission for filling up the aforesaid posts but there is no initiative as yet which is also being represented by Mr. Sanjoy Piprawall, learned counsel appearing for the JSSC."
  },
